"""
Energy-Aware Autoscaling Controller for Kubernetes.

Implements the Energy-Aware Elastic Scaling (EAES) algorithm adapted from
the base research paper (Li et al., 2025, JNCA 10.1016/j.jnca.2025.104218).

The controller considers CPU utilization, request rate, latency, and energy
per request to make scaling decisions for Kubernetes Deployments.

Key Features:
- Feedback control loop enhanced with energy awareness
- SLA-aware scale-up (latency threshold)
- Hysteresis for stable scale-down
- Energy per request estimation (CPU-utilization-based, explicitly labeled)
- Cooldown periods to prevent oscillations
- Minimum and maximum replica limits
- Configurable parameters
- Decision logging
- Kubernetes API integration (real or simulated mode)
"""

